// SURVIVORZ: every downloaded prop that fills a line of docs/survivorz/ASSET-CHECK.md, with
// what it takes to make it game-ready. scripts/survivorz/pack-props.mjs reads this.
//
//   src   "sf:<uid>" (Sketchfab zip in free/sketchfab/) | "ph:<id>" (Poly Haven glTF)
//   fit   how to reach real size: ["m"] the file is already in metres;
//         ["h", 1.7] scale so it stands 1.7 m tall; ["l", 0.9] so its longest side is 0.9 m
//   tier  the triangle and texture budget from ASSETS.md §1:
//         "hero"   ≤ 30k triangles, 2K textures (the camera gets within a metre: beds,
//                  benches, consoles, and everything held in a hand)
//         "prop"   ≤ 8k, 1K (ordinary furniture and pickups seen from further off)
//         "small"  ≤ 2k, 1K (clutter)
//         "kit"    ≤ 30k, 2K (architecture pieces, instanced)
//   mat   material fixes by material name: { name: { color, metal, rough, alpha } }
//   art   { material, image }: our own print in a frame (scripts/survivorz/room-art.mjs draws it)
//   powerOff  true: screens and LEDs painted into the art go dark (the facility has no mains power)
//   note  what to know when it's placed
// Every size below was chosen from the model's measured bounds (in its own units) against
// the real object, then checked against a 1.8 m figure on the props bench.
